      "text": [
        " عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ فَمَنْ لَمْ يَجِدْ فَصِيامُ ثَلاثَةِ أَيَّامٍ فِي الْحَجِّ وَ سَبْعَةٍ إِذا رَجَعْتُمْ تِلْكَ عَشَرَةٌ كامِلَةٌ قَالَ كَمَالُهَا كَمَالُ الْأُضْحِيَّةِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin IBrahimm, from his father, raising it, ",
          "‘Regarding the Words of the Mighty and Majestic <span class=\"ibTxt\"><a href=\"/#/books/quran:2#h196\"><a href=\"/books/quran:2#h196\">[2:196]</a></a> but he who cannot find (any offering) should Fast for three days during the Hajj and for seven days when he returns; these (make) ten (days) complete</span>. He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘Its completion is the completion of the slaughtering’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "15. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from in a marfu‘ manner the following: “This is about the words of Allah, most Majestic, most Glorious, ‘If he cannot find (offering) he must fast three days in al-Hajj and seven days when you return and this becomes ten complete.’ <a href=\"/#/books/quran:2#h196\"><a href=\"/books/quran:2#h196\">[2:196]</a></a> He (the Imam), ‘Alayhi al-Salam, said that completing fasting is completing the offering obligation.’” "
        ]
      }
